$ cat about.txt | fold -w 75

    a minimal reverse-mode autograd engine in c, just big enough to train
    karpathy's microGPT. float64 tensors, a tape walked in reverse, and 12
    ops with forward and backward next to each other.

    correctness by:

    - numeric parity with karpathy's microGPT to within 1e-11 atol
    - a finite-difference gradient check for every op and the full model
    - asan and ubsan on every test run

    discussion on hackernews: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46285424

$ make parity

    trained 1000 steps in 0.256s
    passed parity check (max |diff| 5.7e-15)
    inference (random sampled name): mashrh

see also:

- counterpart in lean: https://github.com/sueszli/autograd.lean
- original microgpt implementation: https://karpathy.github.io/2026/02/12/microgpt/
